  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "A rapid interest rate rise seems inevitable – and households are expected to pick up the tab",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/14/interest-rate-rise-phillip-inman-inflation-economy",
      "description": "<p>Raising borrowing costs too far risks laying waste to whatever growth there is in the economy</p><p>A head of steam is building up behind the Bank of England raising interest rates again. With the latest forecasts by the central bank showing inflation rising to 5% next spring, another increase in the cost of borrowing seems inevitable, and may come as soon as next month.</p><p>A growing number of analysts predict the Bank’s policymakers will don Scrooge masks when they meet on 17 December to deliver a message of austerity and sacrifice.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/14/interest-rate-rise-phillip-inman-inflation-economy\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T16:00:48"
    },
    {
      "title": "Interest rate rises likely in coming months, Bank of England’s chief economist says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/14/interest-rate-rises-inflation-bank-of-england-chief-economist",
      "description": "<p>‘We have further to go,’ says Huw Pill after increase to 4% this month as Bank seeks to tackle rising inflation</p><p>The Bank of England will probably need to raise interest rates next month and again in early 2027 to combat rising inflation, its chief economist has said.</p><p>Signalling a sharp rise in mortgage payments for an estimated <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/nov/02/mortgage-payments-rise-2027-interest-rates\">2.3 million homeowners</a> who will have to refinance their loans next year, Huw Pill said that while the decision to nudge interest rates from 3.75% to 4% earlier this month was a “significant step” towards getting monetary policy into a better place, “we ⁠have further to go”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/14/interest-rate-rises-inflation-bank-of-england-chief-economist\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-14T14:42:27"
    },
